    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "The legality of the emulator software itself is distinct from the legality of the game content it runs.",
      "evidence": "Emulators are tools; their legality depends on whether they infringe on patents or trade dress. However, the question asks about the 'games,' which are the copyrighted content, not the tool.",
