      "reason_rejected": "This would only be true if the user created their own backup from a legally owned cartridge (a gray area often permitted for personal use in some jurisdictions but not universally) or if the games were in the public domain (which they are not). The general case of 'getting games for an emulator' implies downloading from the internet, which is illegal. The 'weakest step' attack on the majority position (that it's illegal) fails because the alternative (legality) relies on a narrow, jurisdiction-specific exception (personal backup) that does not apply to the general act of downloading ROMs, which is the standard interpretation of the question."
